# Check every text file out with LF, on every platform.
#
# The smoke checks assert on exact byte sequences that contain LF — for example
# that the reference demo still leads with `await kit.start();\n  kit.ready();`.
# On a Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` those files arrive with CRLF
# and the assertions fail on a clean tree, so the quality gate cannot run.
#
# Pinning LF fixes that at the source instead of loosening the assertions.
* text=auto eol=lf
